My UML/s390 now runs on 2.6.12-rc4 + incremental patches.

Here are three additional patches for "s390-preparation":

- add-PTRACE_AREA:
   Insert PTRACE_PEEKUSR_AREA and PTRACE_POKEUSR_AREA
   actions into arch/um/kernel/ptrace.c (and remove two
   useless lines)

- execve1-add-ARCH_EXECVE1:
   conditionally add subarch-specific action to execve1

- boot_timer_handler-no-prototye:
   remove prototype for boot_timer_handler from
   kern_util.h, as this header now indirectly is included
   in arch/um/os-Linux/signal.c
   Because of s390's ARCH_SIGHDLR_PARAM not being "int"
   compilation of UML/s390 is broken with the latest
   incrementals.

Unfortunately it's still unclear, what the necessary change
in s390-host will look like. So I don't want to "release"
implemetation of UML/s390 yet.

	Bodo

